  <h2>Superchargers</h2>
  <p>
    Portugal is well covered by the Tesla Supercharger network — V2 (150 kW), V3 (250 kW) and V4 stalls along the main routes. Plug-and-charge works exactly like elsewhere in Europe; billing goes to your Tesla account.
  </p>
  <p>
    See the official map at <a href="https://www.tesla.com/en_gb/findus#/bounds/65,55,34,-11,d?search=supercharger&amp;name=Europe">tesla.com/findus</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Public AC / DC network</h2>
  <p>
    Portugal has a country-wide public charging network called <strong>Mobi.E</strong>. To use it you need to be signed up with a comerciante (retailer) — most operators accept ad-hoc payments via app too. Read the detailed <a href="/english/charging-in-portugal/">Charging in Portugal</a> guide.
  </p>

  <h2>Home charging (if you have friends here)</h2>
  <p>
    Portuguese homes use European Schuko sockets (Type F) and industrial CEE outlets. A Tesla Mobile Connector with the right adapter works with either.
  </p>

  <h2>Community</h2>
  <p>
    The Tesla Club Portugal is a volunteer community. If you're visiting and have questions, drop a note in the <a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/teslaclubportugal">Facebook group</a> — English is welcome.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
